Catching Exception everywhere

This can hide the actual problem. Catch the most specific exception you can meaningfully handle.


##
Empty catch blocks
catch (Exception e) {
}
 
This silently discards failures and makes debugging difficult.

 
Using exceptions for ordinary business decisions

If a value can be validated normally, validate it first. Exceptions should not replace routine control flow.



Losing the original cause

When wrapping an exception, preserve its cause where appropriate:

##
throw new RuntimeException(
    "Unable to process order", e
);
